{"slug":"Troops","title":"Troops","cats":["All stub articles","Stubs"],"headings":[{"id":"Gaining_Troops","text":"Gaining Troops","level":2},{"id":"Gaining_Max_Troops","text":"Gaining Max Troops","level":2},{"id":"See_also","text":"See also","level":2}],"html":"<div role=\"note\" class=\"metadata plainlinks asbox stub\"><table role=\"presentation\"><tbody><tr class=\"noresize\"><td><p class=\"asbox-body\">This article is a stub. You can help the wiki by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"/Troops\">expanding it</a>.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"navbar plainlinks hlist navbar-mini\"><ul><li class=\"nv-view\"><abbr title=\"View this template\">v</abbr></li><li class=\"nv-talk\"><span class=\"wiki-deadlink\"><abbr title=\"Discuss this template\">t</abbr></span></li><li class=\"nv-edit\"><span class=\"wiki-deadlink\"><abbr title=\"Edit this template\">e</abbr></span></li></ul></div></div>\n<p><b>Troops</b> are one of the two main resources in OpenFront, the second being <a href=\"/Gold\" title=\"Gold\">gold</a>. They are used to attack and defend territory.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Gaining_Troops\">Gaining Troops</h2></div>\n<p>Troops are gained every tick (1/10th of a second) with the formula\n</p><p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle toAdd=(10+{\\frac {currentTroops^{0.73}}{4}})*(1-{\\frac {currentTroops}{maxTroops}})}}\">\n  <semantics>\n    <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n      <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n        <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n          <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n            <mi>t</mi>\n            <mi>o</mi>\n            <mi>A</mi>\n            <mi>d</mi>\n            <mi>d</mi>\n            <mo>=</mo>\n            <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n            <mn>10</mn>\n            <mo>+</mo>\n            <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n              <mfrac>\n                <mrow>\n                  <mi>c</mi>\n                  <mi>u</mi>\n                  <mi>r</mi>\n                  <mi>r</mi>\n                  <mi>e</mi>\n                  <mi>n</mi>\n                  <mi>t</mi>\n                  <mi>T</mi>\n                  <mi>r</mi>\n                  <mi>o</mi>\n                  <mi>o</mi>\n                  <mi>p</mi>\n                  <msup>\n                    <mi>s</mi>\n                    <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                      <mn>0.73</mn>\n                    </mrow>\n                  </msup>\n                </mrow>\n                <mn>4</mn>\n              </mfrac>\n            </mrow>\n            <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n            <mo>∗</mo>\n            <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n            <mn>1</mn>\n            <mo>−</mo>\n            <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n              <mfrac>\n                <mrow>\n                  <mi>c</mi>\n                  <mi>u</mi>\n                  <mi>r</mi>\n                  <mi>r</mi>\n                  <mi>e</mi>\n                  <mi>n</mi>\n                  <mi>t</mi>\n                  <mi>T</mi>\n                  <mi>r</mi>\n                  <mi>o</mi>\n                  <mi>o</mi>\n                  <mi>p</mi>\n                  <mi>s</mi>\n                </mrow>\n                <mrow>\n                  <mi>m</mi>\n                  <mi>a</mi>\n                  <mi>x</mi>\n                  <mi>T</mi>\n                  <mi>r</mi>\n                  <mi>o</mi>\n                  <mi>o</mi>\n                  <mi>p</mi>\n                  <mi>s</mi>\n                </mrow>\n              </mfrac>\n            </mrow>\n            <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n          </mstyle>\n        </mrow>\n      </mstyle>\n    </mrow>\n    <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle toAdd=(10+{\\frac {currentTroops^{0.73}}{4}})*(1-{\\frac {currentTroops}{maxTroops}})}}</annotation>\n  </semantics>\n</math></span></span>\n</p><p>If you are at max troops, you will not gain any more.\n</p><p>Deriving this formula tells us that the maximum troop gain rate is achieved at <b>42%</b>, meaning that after this point, troop gain starts slowing down.\n</p><p>You can see your current troop gain in the UI in brackets after your maximum troop count.\n</p><p><a href=\"/Bots\" title=\"Bots\">Bots</a> and <a href=\"/Nations\" title=\"Nations\">Nations</a> modify their troop gain by a modifier based on their type and the game's difficulty.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Gaining_Max_Troops\">Gaining Max Troops</h2></div>\n<p>Maximum troops are calculated based on territory land mass (owned tile count), and city count. And is given by the formula\n</p><p><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle maxTroops=2*(numTilesOwned^{0.6}*1000+50000)+numCitiesOwned*250000}}\">\n  <semantics>\n    <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n      <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n        <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n          <mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\">\n            <mi>m</mi>\n            <mi>a</mi>\n            <mi>x</mi>\n            <mi>T</mi>\n            <mi>r</mi>\n            <mi>o</mi>\n            <mi>o</mi>\n            <mi>p</mi>\n            <mi>s</mi>\n            <mo>=</mo>\n            <mn>2</mn>\n            <mo>∗</mo>\n            <mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo>\n            <mi>n</mi>\n            <mi>u</mi>\n            <mi>m</mi>\n            <mi>T</mi>\n            <mi>i</mi>\n            <mi>l</mi>\n            <mi>e</mi>\n            <mi>s</mi>\n            <mi>O</mi>\n            <mi>w</mi>\n            <mi>n</mi>\n            <mi>e</mi>\n            <msup>\n              <mi>d</mi>\n              <mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                <mn>0.6</mn>\n              </mrow>\n            </msup>\n            <mo>∗</mo>\n            <mn>1000</mn>\n            <mo>+</mo>\n            <mn>50000</mn>\n            <mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo>\n            <mo>+</mo>\n            <mi>n</mi>\n            <mi>u</mi>\n            <mi>m</mi>\n            <mi>C</mi>\n            <mi>i</mi>\n            <mi>t</mi>\n            <mi>i</mi>\n            <mi>e</mi>\n            <mi>s</mi>\n            <mi>O</mi>\n            <mi>w</mi>\n            <mi>n</mi>\n            <mi>e</mi>\n            <mi>d</mi>\n            <mo>∗</mo>\n            <mn>250000</mn>\n          </mstyle>\n        </mrow>\n      </mstyle>\n    </mrow>\n    <annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle {\\displaystyle maxTroops=2*(numTilesOwned^{0.6}*1000+50000)+numCitiesOwned*250000}}</annotation>\n  </semantics>\n</math></span></span>\n</p><p>The <b>Infinite Troops</b> setting (available in <a href=\"/Single_Player\" class=\"\" title=\"Singleplayer\">Singleplayer</a> and private lobbies) sets the maximum to 1000000000 (though in game, it is only shown as 100M).\n</p><p>Bots and Nations modify their max troops based on their type and the game's difficulty.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"See_also\">See also</h2></div>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/Combat\" title=\"Combat\">Combat</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/Transport_Ship\" title=\"Transport Ship\">Transport Ship</a></li></ul>","section":"Units"}
